      "text": "Square both sides:\n\\begin{align*}\n\\left(x - \\frac{1}{x}\\right)^2 &= 4^2 \\\\\nx^2 - 2\\cdot 4 \\cdot \\frac{1}{x} + \\frac{1}{x^2} &= 16 \\\\\nx^2 + \\frac{1}{x^2} - 8 &= 16 \\\\\nx^2 + \\frac{1}{x^2} &= 24\n\\end{align*}\n\nNext, to find $x^3 - \\frac{1}{x^3}$, we use the identity:\n\\begin{align*}\nx^3 - \\frac{1}{x^3} &= \\left(x^2 + \\frac{1}{x^2}\\right)\\left(x - \\frac{1}{x}\\right) - \\left(x + \\frac{1}{x}\\right) \\\\\n&= 24\\cdot 4 - \\left(x + \\frac{1}{x}\\right) \\\\\n&= 96 - \\left(x + \\frac{1}{x}\\right)\n\\end{align*}\n\nRecall that $x - \\frac{1}{x} = 4$. \nThus, $x + \\frac{1}{x} = - \\frac{1}{4}$.\n\nTherefore,\n\\begin{align*}\nx^3 - \\frac{1}{x^3} &= 96 - \\left(x + \\frac{1}{x}\\right) \\\\\n&= 96 - \\left(-\\frac{1}{4}\\right) \\\\\n&= 96 + \\frac{1}{4} \\\\\n&= \\boxed{\\frac{385}{4}}.\n\\end{align*}\n\nTherefore, $x^3 - \\frac{1}{x^3} = \\frac{385}{4}$. The final answer is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{385}{4}}\\).",
